    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Across the whole packet, participant experience follows one dominant pattern shown by the cited source.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_4756c6b1b6c944f1\",\"quote\":\"Yes, someone like me helped out of goodwill and still helping as we speak. Being that I am married with children in my home, it is my duty to help girls because maybe I don’t know wat lies ahead as I don’t know who might help my child sometime tomorrow. Suppose you meet a young girl along the road or sick and lying on the roadside, you have just to help her reach the hospital and…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_74c4ede516cd991a\",\"quote\":\"Yes. These things also come from the dress code …there is a bill that was passed in Kenya that made my dress my choice but girls interpreted it the wrong way. That is also causing a lot of problems for us. The skirt that a child has worn even if you didn’t have an interest, it will change your mind to an extent. So, that should also be controlled to an extent.”}],\"\n    }],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet\",\"mechanism\":\"Drawing a single dominant pattern from diverse participant accounts is unwarranted given the fragmented and context-dependent nature of the provided evidence.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely suggests a uniform participant experience, ignoring the varied motivations and circumstances presented across the sources.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence demonstrates a range of motivations, including familial duty, concern for a specific individual, and responses to complex social issues like prostitution and dress code interpretations. \"}\n    ],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence presents conflicting accounts and lacks a unifying pattern to support the claim of a single dominant participant experience. The claim is an unsupported inference.\"}",
